§ `Days of remembrance: § 6720, from the Sunday before April 24 through the following Sunday`

-- 2026-04-24 is a Friday: Sunday before is 19 April, the following Sunday is 26 April.  2025-04-24 is a Thursday: 20 and 27 April.
#ASSERT `the days the Governor is directed to proclaim under` "6720" `in the year` 2026 `given the day of the astronomical Northward equinox:` NOTHING EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 4 19), (YMD 2026 4 26)
#ASSERT `the days the Governor is directed to proclaim under` "6720" `in the year` 2025 `given the day of the astronomical Northward equinox:` NOTHING EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2025 4 20), (YMD 2025 4 27)
-- 2022-04-24 was a Sunday: the text does not say whether that day is the Sunday meant.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the days the Governor is directed to proclaim under` "6720" `in the year` 2022 `given the day of the astronomical Northward equinox:` NOTHING

§ `The astronomical Northward equinox: § 6727 does not compute it`

#ASSERT `the days the Governor is directed to proclaim under` "6727" `in the year` 2026 `given the day of the astronomical Northward equinox:` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 20)) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 20), (YMD 2026 3 20)
#ASSERT `the days the Governor is directed to proclaim under` "6727" `in the year` 2026 `given the day of the astronomical Northward equinox:` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 21)) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 21), (YMD 2026 3 21)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the days the Governor is directed to proclaim under` "6727" `in the year` 2026 `given the day of the astronomical Northward equinox:` NOTHING

