§ `Whether the duty recurs each year (fork F-proclaim-once)`

-- §§ 6708-6711 say "shall proclaim" a day "to be known hereafter" and do not say annually.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the section directs a proclamation every year` "6708"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the section directs a proclamation every year` "6709"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the section directs a proclamation every year` "6710"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the section directs a proclamation every year` "6711"
-- The others say annually, each year, of each year or annually be so proclaimed.
#ASSERT `the section directs a proclamation every year` "6712"
#ASSERT `the section directs a proclamation every year` "6713"
#ASSERT `the section directs a proclamation every year` "6718"
#ASSERT `the section directs a proclamation every year` "6719"
#ASSERT `the section directs a proclamation every year` "6720"
#ASSERT `the section directs a proclamation every year` "6726"
#ASSERT `the section directs a proclamation every year` "6727"
#ASSERT `the section directs a proclamation every year` "6731"
#ASSERT `the section directs a proclamation every year` "6736"

§ `Whether a proclamation makes a holiday (fork F-hol-6)`

#ASSERT REFUSED `a proclamation under the section makes the day a holiday` "6709"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a proclamation under the section makes the day a holiday` "6736"
-- Gov. Code § 6709 proclaims 15 January; the holiday is the third Monday in January (§ 6700(a)(3)): 19 January 2026 is a holiday and 15 January 2026 is not.
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(3) makes the day a holiday` (YMD 2026 1 19)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 6700(a)(3) makes the day a holiday` (YMD 2026 1 15))

§ `Gov. Code § 6726: Space Day`

#ASSERT NOT (`a school, educational institution, resident, business or public entity is required to take part in Space Day`)
#ASSERT `the Governor is to direct the Department of General Services to turn off the light on Space Day` `a nonessential light`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Governor is to direct the Department of General Services to turn off the light on Space Day` `an essential light`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      secs IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Moment
`the moment on` d `at` secs MEANS
    Moment WITH
        `the day` IS d
        `seconds after midnight` IS secs

-- Between 9 p.m. (75,600 seconds after midnight) and 10 p.m. (79,200) on Space Day: 1 May 2026.
#ASSERT `the moment falls in the lights-out hour of Space Day` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `at` 77400) `of the year` 2026
#ASSERT `the moment falls in the lights-out hour of Space Day` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `at` 75601) `of the year` 2026
#ASSERT `the moment falls in the lights-out hour of Space Day` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `at` 79199) `of the year` 2026
#ASSERT NOT (`the moment falls in the lights-out hour of Space Day` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `at` 75599) `of the year` 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`the moment falls in the lights-out hour of Space Day` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `at` 79201) `of the year` 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`the moment falls in the lights-out hour of Space Day` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `at` 0) `of the year` 2026)
-- The instants of 9 p.m. and 10 p.m. themselves: the text says between, and does not say whether the ends are inside.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the moment falls in the lights-out hour of Space Day` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `at` 75600) `of the year` 2026
#ASSERT REFUSED `the moment falls in the lights-out hour of Space Day` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `at` 79200) `of the year` 2026
-- Not Space Day: the next Friday, and the first Friday of the next year's May.
#ASSERT NOT (`the moment falls in the lights-out hour of Space Day` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 5 8) `at` 77400) `of the year` 2026)
#ASSERT `the moment falls in the lights-out hour of Space Day` (`the moment on` (YMD 2027 5 7) `at` 77400) `of the year` 2027

